# ovh_dedicated_cloud_user (Resource)

Manage a VMware on OVHcloud (dedicatedCloud/PCC) user.

## Example Usage

{{tffile "examples/resources/dedicated_cloud_user/example_1.tf"}}

<!-- schema generated by tfplugindocs -->
## Schema

### Required

- `name` (String) Name of the user
- `service_name` (String) The internal name of your VMware on OVHcloud

### Optional

- `can_add_ressource` (Boolean) Default right given at creation to the user to add ressources in your VMware on OVHcloud. Not returned by the API: changing it outside of Terraform will not be detected
- `can_manage_ip_fail_overs` (Boolean) Defines if the user can manage ip failovers
- `can_manage_network` (Boolean) Defines if the user can manage the network
- `can_manage_rights` (Boolean) Defines if the user can manage users rights
- `email` (String) Email address of the user
- `encryption_right` (Boolean) Defines if the user can manage encryption / KMS configuration
- `expiration_date` (String) Expiration date of the user account (RFC3339 datetime). Not returned by the API: changing it outside of Terraform will not be detected
- `first_name` (String) First name of the user
- `full_admin_ro` (Boolean) Defines if the user is a full admin in readonly
- `is_token_validator` (Boolean) Defines if the user can confirm security tokens (if a compatible option is enabled)
- `last_name` (String) Last name of the user
- `network_role` (String) Default network role given at creation to the user on every existing datacenter of your VMware on OVHcloud. Not returned by the API: changing it outside of Terraform will not be detected
- `nsx_right` (Boolean) Is this User able to access nsx interface (requires NSX option)
- `password` (String, Sensitive) Password of the user. Not returned by the API: changing it outside of Terraform will not be detected
- `phone_number` (String) Mobile phone number of the user
- `receive_alerts` (Boolean) Defines if the user receives technical alerts
- `right` (String) Default right given at creation to the user on every existing datacenter of your VMware on OVHcloud. Not returned by the API: changing it outside of Terraform will not be detected
- `vm_network_role` (String) Default VM network role given at creation to the user on every existing datacenter of your VMware on OVHcloud. Not returned by the API: changing it outside of Terraform will not be detected

### Read-Only

- `activation_state` (String) Activation state of the user account
- `id` (String) Unique identifier for the resource
- `identity_provider_id` (Number) Linked Identity Provider (if any), can be Federation Active Directory or IAM
- `identity_provider_type` (String) Linked Identity Provider type (if any), can be Federation Active Directory or IAM
- `is_enable_manageable` (Boolean) Check if the given VMware on OVHcloud user can be enabled or disabled
- `login` (String) Login of the user
- `state` (String) State of the user account
- `type` (String) User type (if any)
- `user_id` (Number) Id of the user

## Import

A dedicated cloud user can be imported using the `service_name` and the `user_id`, separated by "/" E.g.,

```bash
$ terraform import ovh_dedicated_cloud_user.john "<service_name>/<user_id>"
```

~> Fields not returned by the read API (`password`, `right`, `network_role`, `vm_network_role`, `can_add_ressource`, `expiration_date`) will be empty after import.
